# race2p.press with player 1's view alone across the frame (RUSH_GFX_VIEW=1, as net.view = own shows the host's in
# an online session; docs/port/NETPLAY.md 14): render-only, so the same course as race2p, and the screenshot one view
# across the frame, where the split screen's divider, side panel and left border were dark.
# until: 0x400000:600
# seconds: 90
# expect: state=0x00400000: players 2, windows 2, cars 6, mode 0, track 0
# env: RUSH_GFX_VIEW=1
# args: --screenshot-at 1300 --screenshot race2pown.png
# check: tools/port/synth_shot.py race2pown.png own
5 A            # the controller pak warning
8 START        # the start prompt
9 RIGHT 0.1    # the main menu's first option: one player more (as many as controllers)
11 A           # the main menu: the race
14 A           # the player screen: each player is ready
14 A@2
17 A           # the mode screen: a single race
20 A           # the track select: track 0
23 A           # the car select: each player's car
23 A@2
